%N A113254 Corresponds to m = 8 in a family of 4th-order linear recurrence sequences given by a(n) = m^4*a(n-4) + (2*m)^2*a(n-3) - 4*a(n-1), a(0) = -1, a(1) = 4, a(2) = -13 + 6*(m-1) + 3*(m-1)^2, a(3) = (-8+m^2)^2.
%C A113254 Conjecture: a(m, 2*n+1) is a perfect square for all m,n (see A113249).
%C A113254 This was proved in the case m = 8 (this sequence) by an autonomous AI agent, see the Lean file. The proof uses an auxiliary sequence Y (a second-order recurrence) and shows the odd-indexed terms satisfy a(2n+1) = Y(n)^2 by induction over a three-term window. - _Ralf Stephan_, May 25 2026
%H A113254 Colin Barker, <a href="/A113254/b113254.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1000</a>
%H A113254 Google Deepmind, <a href="https://github.com/google-deepmind/alphaproof-nexus-results/blob/main/APNOutputs/OEIS/oeis_113254_conjecture_0.lean">AlphaProof Nexus: A113254 Lean file</a>
%H A113254 <a href="/index/Rec#order_04">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (-4,0,256,4096).
%F A113254 G.f.: (-1+192*x^2+4096*x^3) / ((8*x+1)*(1-8*x)*(64*x^2+4*x+1)).
%F A113254 a(n) = -4*a(n-1) + 256*a(n-3) + 4096*a(n-4) for n > 3. - _Colin Barker_, May 20 2019
%F A113254 E.g.f.: 4*sinh(8*x) - exp(-2*x)*(cos(2*sqrt(15)*x) + sqrt(15)*sin(2*sqrt(15)*x)). - _Stefano Spezia_, Aug 15 2026
%t A113254 LinearRecurrence[{-4, 0, 256, 4096}, {-1, 4, 176, 3136}, 25] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Jun 10 2024 *)
%o A113254 (PARI) Vec(-(1 - 192*x^2 - 4096*x^3) / ((1 - 8*x)*(1 + 8*x)*(1 + 4*x + 64*x^2)) + O(x^25)) \\ _Colin Barker_, May 20 2019
%Y A113254 Cf. A000302, A097948, A056450, A113249, A113250, A113251, A113252, A113253, A113255, A113256.
